### Manual API testing.
### Install the "REST Client" VS Code extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### Cookies are remembered between requests, just like a browser.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### Sign up
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Abhay",
  "lastName": "Nath",
  "emailId": "abhay@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### Log in
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emailId": "abhay@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### My profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/profile

### Update profile
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "about": "Learning Node.js",
  "skills": ["node", "express", "mongodb"],
  "age": 25
}

### Change password
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/profile/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Password123",
  "newPassword": "Password456"
}

### Feed (paginated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/feed?page=1&limit=10

### Send a request (replace the id with a user id from the feed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/requests/send/interested/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID

### Requests I received
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/requests/received

### Accept a request (replace with a request id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/requests/review/accepted/REPLACE_WITH_REQUEST_ID

### My connections
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/connections

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
